### Rework round 2 — ARCH-REV-S02-r2's verdict, applied (2026-09-06; `SPEC.md` v3 still frozen and untouched, md5 `ad060bda81db71f00f4c70b1dbf63f2f`, verified at CLAIM and at handoff)

- 2026-09-06 · **B3 — the frozen SPEC's R17 cases 4 and 5 contradict its own R05, and the B1 fix is what exposed it** · **RECORDED, ROUTED, AND PLANNED AT V-18's DEFAULT (a): the two cases keep their step ids and the PROPERTY they assert ("both boxes checked → `Create account` NOT `disabled`"), and only the ROUTE changes — from a bare `field("privacy-accepted").click()` to the modal's acknowledgement (open the policy from the unchecked row, satisfy `S02-S40`'s scroll gate, activate `I have read it`), which is the same route `S02-S52`/`S02-S53` already use. The frozen SPEC text is NOT edited.** · The contradiction is internal to the SPEC and not a plan defect: `SPEC.md:370-372` says cases 1-4 run "from a fresh mount with the one idiom" (`field(name).click()`), while R05 — and V's goal verbatim at `SPEC.md:133-134`, *"if the User does not click the I agree button, then the tickbox is not ticked"* — require a bare click on the EMPTY privacy box to open the policy and leave the box empty. **Any implementation satisfying case 4 literally must tick the box on a bare click, which is the one behaviour V's goal forbids.** Nobody could see it before this round for two measured reasons: (1) the round-0 mirror desync (B1) set the R17 mirror `true` while the DOM said `false`, so the two cases passed by accident — measured `STAGE c7-unfixed: 6/6 pass` against `STAGE c7: 4/6 pass` on the same probe; (2) the N7 chain rule, added in round 1, is what first put `consent-signup-gate.test.tsx` inside C7's own verification command · **Measured, three invocations, identical:** `node .hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/arch-s02-rework-r2-r17-post-c7-fixed.mjs` → `STAGE c7: 6/6 pass, 0 FAIL` · V row **V-18**, ticket `t_d12339f3` · ARCH-S02-REWORK-R2 (finding B3), routed to V

- 2026-09-06 · **B3 — where cases 4 and 5 LIVE, now that their route needs the modal** · **They move from cluster `S02-C4` to `S02-C7`, and from `tests/render/consent-signup-gate.test.tsx` to `tests/render/consent-signup-modal.test.tsx`, which C7 creates and owns. `S02-C4` goes 8 steps → 6, `S02-C7` goes 11 → 13; NO step is renumbered, no requirement loses a step (R17's trace row already read `C4 · C7`), and NO cluster's file count changes — C4 still runs 4 files, C7 still 5, C9 still 10.** · Forced by measurement, not preference: at the C4 stage the component has no row handler and no modal, so the acknowledgement route reports `NO MODAL AT THIS STAGE` and the cases are unsatisfiable there (`STAGE c4: 4/6 pass, 2 FAIL`, three runs) · The two steps are written out PHYSICALLY inside `§Cluster S02-C7`, after `S02-S71`, because `arch-rev-s02-trace.py` groups steps by the `### Cluster` heading they sit under: a step whose body said `Cluster **C7**` while sitting in C4's section would be counted in C4 and the two statements would silently disagree — the B4 class · Re-measured after the move: `S02-C4 6 · S02-C7 13 · total: 72`, `distinct step ids appearing in the trace table: 72`, `DEFINED steps that appear in NO trace row: []`, `refutation-table rows: 72` · ARCH-S02-REWORK-R2 (finding B3)

- 2026-09-06 · **B3 — the rejected alternatives, each with the measurement that rejected it** (`COMMON.md` §10.1; `superpowers:brainstorming` was loaded THIS session before the direction was settled) · **ALT-2 "keep case 4's bare `.click()` and exempt C7 from running the gate file" — REJECTED, measured** (`node .hermes/reports/consent-ui/probes/arch-s02-rework-r2-alternatives.mjs`, three runs identical): the only rule under which the literal case can pass is one where a bare click ticks the empty box, and under it `bare click ticked box=true btnDisabled=false acknowledgements=0 register()=1` — a registration with the policy never opened. The pinned rule on the identical keystrokes gives `ticked box=false btnDisabled=true register()=0 dialogOpen=true`. It also re-opens N7, whose chain arm is the only thing making C7 RED at base · **ALT-3 "reach both-checked by assignment, no modal needed" — REJECTED, measured:** `assignment-only route: btnDisabled=true` — an assignment never reaches React, so the case is unsatisfiable at every stage, in C4 and C7 alike · **ALT-4 "leave both cases in `consent-signup-gate.test.tsx` and let the C7 seat append to it" — REJECTED on the boundary, not on a measurement:** it would require amending §Per-cluster boundaries so C7 may WRITE a file C4 owns, weakening the "RUNNING a test file is not WRITING it" rule the reviewer called correct, and it would make a red in that file ambiguous between "C7's new case" and "C7 regressed C4" — the exact discrimination the chain arm exists to provide · **ALT-5 "give C7 a third test file for the two cases" — REJECTED on cost:** it takes C7's `Test Files` arm 5 → 6 and C9's 10 → 11 for two cases, and fragments R17 across three files instead of two · **Accepted cost of the chosen option, stated because it is a real loss:** R17's six cases now live in two files rather than one · ARCH-S02-REWORK-R2 (finding B3)

